    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XtewvJNLFivhp9zuT97jG8)_\n\n## What\n`org-clock-in` signalled `Wrong number of arguments` because `sp-modeline-parts-clock-switch-state` took no arguments, but Org calls `org-clock-in-switch-to-state` with one: the entry's current todo keyword (or nil). The function now takes `&optional state`, uses it instead of reading point, and returns the clock keyword only when the entry has an open keyword and the configured keyword is in `org-todo-keywords-1`. Behaviour is otherwise unchanged. The other clock hooks (`-flag`, `-unflag`) are called with no arguments by Org, so they are fine. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The call signature is from my memory of `org-clock.el`, not checked against the Org version installed on your machine.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi97xXZoCjrZuTnZKXZ)_",
